BT /F2 16 Tf 54 723 Td (Tessera TS-4 Gateway Installation Guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 701 Td (Document ID: prod-ts4-gateway-installation-guide | Version: 4.2 | Effective: 2025-08-25 |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 688 Td (Owner: Tessera Product Engineering, Meridian Instruments Ltd) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 663 Td (1. About this guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641 Td (This guide describes how to survey, mount, power, connect and commission the Tessera TS-4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 628 Td (gateway, and how to pair TS-4e edge nodes to it. It applies to both gateway variants:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 615 Td (TS4-GW-LTE \(LTE Cat-M1 plus Ethernet backhaul\) and TS4-GW-ETH \(Ethernet-only backhaul\). Where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 602 Td (the procedure differs between the two variants, the difference is called out explicitly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 580 Td (The procedures in this edition assume gateway firmware 5.3.0, released on 18 August 2025.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 567 Td (Earlier firmware \(5.1.x and 5.2.x\) uses the same menu structure for most tasks, but the mesh) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 554 Td (channel planner described in section 11 and the gland kit guidance in section 12 were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541 Td (introduced or revised with 5.3.0. For the firmware versions supported with each TS-4e edge node) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528 Td (release, refer to the Tessera Firmware Compatibility Matrix) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 515 Td (\(prod-tessera-firmware-compatibility-matrix\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493 Td (This guide is intended for Meridian field engineers, certified Tessera partners and customer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 480 Td (maintenance technicians who have completed the Tessera Installer module. Only qualified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 467 Td (personnel should open the gateway enclosure or work on the power supply.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 442 Td (2. Safety information) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 420 Td (The TS-4 gateway is not certified for use in hazardous areas. It must be installed in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 407 Td (non-classified \(safe\) area. TS-4e edge nodes in the Zone 2 variant \(TS4E-NODE-3AX-Z2\) may be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 394 Td (installed inside a Zone 2 area, but the gateway they report to must remain outside the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 381 Td (classified boundary. Radio range through a hazardous-area boundary wall should be verified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368 Td (during the site survey.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (Observe the following precautions:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 324 Td (- Isolate the power supply before opening the enclosure lid. Where the gateway is powered by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 311 Td (   Power over Ethernet, disconnect the Ethernet cable at the switch or injector.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298 Td (- Do not install the LTE antenna within 20 cm of locations normally occupied by people, in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 285 Td (   order to comply with RF exposure limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272 Td (- When working at height, follow the site's permit-to-work and fall-protection rules. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 259 Td (   gateway weighs 1.9 kg with the mounting bracket fitted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 246 Td (- The internal lithium coin cell \(real-time clock backup\) is not user-replaceable.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 230 Td (3. Site survey) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 208 Td (A site survey is required before any gateway is mounted. The survey confirms backhaul) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 195 Td (availability, mesh radio coverage and a suitable mounting position. Meridian recommends using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 182 Td (the TesseraSurvey mobile app with a demo gateway from a Meridian demo kit, although a manual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 169 Td (survey is acceptable for small installations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 147 Td (Check the following during the survey:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 125 Td (- Backhaul: for TS4-GW-LTE, confirm LTE Cat-M1 coverage with a minimum RSRP of -110 dBm at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 112 Td (   the proposed antenna position. For TS4-GW-ETH, confirm a switch port within 100 m of cable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 99 Td (   length and whether it supplies PoE \(IEEE 802.3at\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 86 Td (- Firewall: the gateway requires outbound TCP 443 \(HTTPS\) and TCP 8883 \(MQTT over TLS\) to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 73 Td (   *.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com, and outbound UDP 123 for NTP. No inbound ports) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 60 Td (   are required.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
