6 0 obj
<< /Length 4604 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (- Mesh coverage: TesseraMesh operates in the 2.4 GHz band using IEEE 802.15.4. Typical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   line-of-sight range between nodes is 80 m indoors in open plant rooms and 200 m outdoors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   Dense steelwork, tank walls and concrete bunds reduce range significantly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (- Node count: one gateway supports up to 64 TS-4e edge nodes. For more nodes, plan an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   additional gateway per group of 64 nodes and assign each to a separate mesh network ID.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (- Wi-Fi coexistence: record the channels used by existing 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi access points so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (   that the mesh channel can be planned to avoid them \(see section 11\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (Record the survey results on form TS-F-012 \(Tessera Site Survey Record\) and attach it to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (installation work order.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 600 Td (4. Mounting the gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 578 Td (The TS-4 gateway is supplied with a stainless steel wall and pole bracket \(part TS4-BRK-01\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 565 Td (The enclosure is rated IP66 and may be installed outdoors, but should be shielded from direct) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 552 Td (sunlight where ambient temperatures regularly exceed 50 C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 530 Td (To mount the gateway on a wall:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 508 Td (1. Choose a position at least 2 m above floor level and at least 1 m away from large metal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 495 Td (   obstructions, with the antenna ports facing upwards or sideways, never downwards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 482 Td (2. Mark and drill the four bracket holes using the bracket as a template. On concrete or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 469 Td (   masonry, use M8 anchors rated for at least 0.5 kN pull-out load.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 456 Td (3. Fix the bracket with the four M8 bolts supplied and tighten them to 12 N m. Do not exceed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 443 Td (   15 N m, as over-tightening can distort the bracket and stress the enclosure base.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (4. Hang the gateway on the bracket hooks and secure it with the two M5 locking screws,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417 Td (   tightened to 3 N m.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 404 Td (5. Fit the earth bonding lead from the enclosure earth stud to a local protective earth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 391 Td (   point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 378 Td (For pole mounting, use the two stainless steel band clamps included with TS4-BRK-01. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 365 Td (bracket accepts poles from 40 mm to 110 mm in diameter.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 340 Td (5. Antennas) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318 Td (Each gateway ships with a 2.4 GHz mesh antenna \(TS4-ANT-MESH, 5 dBi omnidirectional\). The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 305 Td (TS4-GW-LTE variant additionally ships with an LTE antenna \(TS4-ANT-LTE, 3 dBi, 698-2690 MHz\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 292 Td (Both antennas use N-type connectors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 270 Td (- Hand-tighten each N-type connector, then tighten to 1.7 N m using a torque spanner.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 257 Td (   Over-tightening damages the connector centre pin.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 244 Td (- Where antennas are mounted remotely, use low-loss cable \(LMR-400 or equivalent\) and keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 231 Td (   the run under 10 m. Every remote antenna run must include a coaxial lightning arrestor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 218 Td (   \(TS4-LPA-01\) bonded to the site earth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 205 Td (- Seal outdoor connector joints with self-amalgamating tape, then a layer of UV-resistant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192 Td (   PVC tape.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179 Td (- The mesh and LTE antennas must be at least 30 cm apart to avoid desensitisation of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 166 Td (   mesh receiver.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 150 Td (6. Power) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 128 Td (The gateway can be powered in two ways. Do not connect both sources at the same time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 106 Td (- Power over Ethernet: the Ethernet port \(ETH0\) accepts IEEE 802.3at \(PoE+, Type 2\) power.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 93 Td (   IEEE 802.3af \(Type 1\) is not sufficient when the LTE modem is active. Maximum cable length) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 80 Td (   is 100 m.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 67 Td (- DC supply: the terminal block TB1 accepts 10-30 VDC. Typical consumption is 6.5 W, peak 11) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 54 Td (   W during LTE transmission. Use a supply rated for at least 15 W and a 2 A slow-blow fuse) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
