stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   in the positive line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (The gateway includes a supercapacitor hold-up that keeps the processor running for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (approximately 20 seconds after power loss, which is sufficient to flush buffered readings to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (flash memory and log a clean shutdown event. A power loss that exceeds this period is logged as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (event code T-320 only if backhaul is also lost; a clean power loss is reported in TesseraCloud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (as "Gateway powered down".) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 639 Td (7. Backhaul configuration) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 616 Td (7.1 Ethernet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 594 Td (By default ETH0 uses DHCP. To set a static address, open the local web interface \(section 8\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 581 Td (and go to Network > Ethernet > IPv4, select Static, and enter the address, netmask, gateway and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 568 Td (DNS servers. Proxy servers are supported for HTTPS traffic \(Network > Proxy\), but the MQTT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555 Td (connection on TCP 8883 cannot be proxied; if the site requires all traffic through a proxy,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542 Td (enable "MQTT over WebSocket" on the same page, which tunnels telemetry over TCP 443.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 519 Td (7.2 LTE \(TS4-GW-LTE only\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 497 Td (The TS4-GW-LTE uses a nano-SIM \(4FF\) inserted in the slot under the lid, beside the terminal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 484 Td (block. Meridian supplies a pre-activated global IoT SIM \(TS4-SIM-GLB\) as an option;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 471 Td (customer-supplied SIMs must support LTE Cat-M1 on the local network.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 449 Td (1. Isolate power and open the lid.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 436 Td (2. Insert the SIM with the notched corner towards the hinge until it clicks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423 Td (3. Close the lid, restore power and open the local interface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 410 Td (4. Go to Network > Cellular > APN and enter the APN, and the username and password if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397 Td (   operator requires them. The TS4-SIM-GLB uses the APN "meridian.iot".) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 384 Td (5. Set the backhaul priority at Network > Backhaul Priority. The default is Ethernet first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371 Td (   with LTE as failover. Failover occurs after 90 seconds without an Ethernet route to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 358 Td (   TesseraCloud.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 342 Td (8. Local web interface) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 320 Td (The local web interface is used for initial configuration and for troubleshooting when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 307 Td (gateway cannot reach TesseraCloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 285 Td (- Connect a laptop to the service port \(the second RJ45 port, labelled SVC\). The service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272 Td (   port runs a DHCP server and assigns the laptop an address in 192.168.50.0/24.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 259 Td (- Browse to https://192.168.50.1. The certificate is self-signed; accept the browser) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 246 Td (   warning.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 233 Td (- Log in as user "admin" with the unique initial password printed on the rating label inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 220 Td (   the lid. You will be required to change it at first login. The new password must be at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207 Td (   least 12 characters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 194 Td (- The session times out after 15 minutes of inactivity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 181 Td (The local interface is disabled on the ETH0 \(backhaul\) port by default. It can be enabled at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 168 Td (System > Access > Local UI on ETH0, but Meridian advises against this on shared corporate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 155 Td (networks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 130 Td (9. Registering the gateway in TesseraCloud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 108 Td (Before the gateway can forward data, it must be claimed into a TesseraCloud tenant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 86 Td (1. In TesseraCloud, a user with the Site Admin or Tenant Owner role opens Fleet > Gateways >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 73 Td (   Add Gateway.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 60 Td (2. Enter the gateway serial number \(format TS4G-YYWW-NNNNN, printed on the rating label\) and) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 3 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 8 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 4364 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   the 8-character claim code on the same label.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (3. Select the site the gateway belongs to. Gateways can later be moved between sites using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   Transfer Site, described in the TesseraCloud Administrator Guide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (4. The gateway downloads its device certificate and appears as "Online" within approximately) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   2 minutes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (If the gateway does not appear online, check the Status > Cloud page in the local interface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (The most common causes are blocked outbound TCP 8883, an incorrect APN, or incorrect system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (time preventing TLS validation \(see section 13\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 613 Td (10. Commissioning the mesh and pairing edge nodes) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 590 Td (10.1 Creating the mesh network) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 568 Td (At first boot the gateway generates a random 16-bit mesh network ID and a network key. The mesh) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555 Td (network ID is shown at Mesh > Overview. If several gateways are installed on the same site,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542 Td (confirm that each has a distinct network ID; this is automatic in almost all cases, but a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 529 Td (collision can be resolved with Mesh > Overview > Regenerate Network ID. Regenerating the ID) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 516 Td (unpairs all nodes.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 493 Td (10.2 Pairing TS-4e edge nodes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 471 Td (TS-4e edge nodes ship in a deep-sleep state to preserve their battery. To pair a node:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 449 Td (1. In TesseraCloud open the site, then Fleet > Gateways > [gateway] > Nodes > Pair Nodes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 436 Td (   This opens a 10-minute pairing window on the gateway. Alternatively, open the window) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423 Td (   locally at Mesh > Pairing > Open Window.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 410 Td (2. Wake each node by holding a magnet \(supplied with the node\) against the marked spot on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 397 Td (   node housing for 3 seconds. The node LED flashes green while searching.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 384 Td (3. The node joins, the LED shows a solid green for 5 seconds, and the node appears in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 371 Td (   node list with its serial number \(TS4E-YYWW-NNNNN\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 358 Td (4. Assign each node to an asset and measurement point in TesseraCloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 345 Td (A node that fails to join within the window reports T-301 \(node not joined\) once the gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332 Td (sees its beacon. Refer to the Tessera Error Code Reference \(sup-tessera-error-codes\) for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319 Td (causes. The most common cause is a node firmware version that the gateway does not support; for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 306 Td (example, a node running 2.8.0 will not join a gateway on 5.2.x.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 283 Td (10.3 Mounting edge nodes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 261 Td (TS-4e nodes mount on an M6 stud. The stud must be tightened into the machine surface first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248 Td (then the node is screwed onto the stud and tightened to 6 N m. Detailed mounting guidance,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 235 Td (including spot-facing and adhesive mounting pads, is in the TS-4e datasheet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (\(prod-ts4e-edge-node-datasheet\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 197 Td (11. Mesh radio planning and advanced mesh settings) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 175 Td (The default mesh configuration suits most installations. The settings in this section should) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 162 Td (only be changed after a site survey has shown a need.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 139 Td (11.1 Channel plan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 117 Td (TesseraMesh uses IEEE 802.15.4 channels 11 to 26 in the 2.4 GHz band. The factory default) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 104 Td (channel is 15, chosen because it falls between Wi-Fi channels 1 and 6. If the survey shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 91 Td (heavy Wi-Fi use on channels 1 and 6, channel 25 or 26 usually gives the cleanest spectrum; note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 78 Td (that channel 26 is restricted to reduced transmit power in some regions and is not available on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 65 Td (units sold in certain markets.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 3 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 10 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R >> >> >>
