12 0 obj
<< /Length 4163 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (To change the channel, go to Mesh > Radio > Channel Plan in the local interface, or Fleet >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (Gateways > [gateway] > Mesh > Radio in TesseraCloud. Select either a fixed channel or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td ("Adaptive", which lets the gateway move between up to four channels you nominate. When the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (channel changes, the gateway broadcasts the change to all paired nodes over the next three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (beacon cycles, which takes up to 3 minutes. Nodes that are asleep or out of range during this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (period will reappear with T-301 and must be re-paired.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 641 Td (11.2 Hop count and topology) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619 Td (TesseraMesh is a self-forming mesh. Nodes may relay messages for other nodes. The maximum hop) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 606 Td (count from any node to the gateway is 4. A node that can only reach the gateway through more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 593 Td (than 4 hops will not join, and will report T-301. Meridian recommends designing for no more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 580 Td (than 3 hops, leaving a spare hop for route recovery when a relay node fails.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (For network stability, no more than 24 nodes should connect directly to the gateway \(first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 545 Td (hop\). Above that number, some nodes should be positioned so that they route through neighbours.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 522 Td (11.3 Transmit power) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500 Td (The mesh transmit power is set at Mesh > Radio > TX Power. The default is +8 dBm. It may be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487 Td (raised to a maximum of +10 dBm where regional regulations permit. Raising transmit power) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 474 Td (increases range but also reduces TS-4e battery life on nodes that relay traffic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 451 Td (11.4 Beacon and reporting intervals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 429 Td (The gateway beacon interval is fixed at 60 seconds. The node reporting interval is set per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416 Td (asset in TesseraCloud. At the default of 1 sample per hour, the TS-4e battery lasts 5 years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 403 Td (Faster reporting intervals shorten battery life proportionally.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 378 Td (12. Enclosure, cable entries and environmental limits) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 355 Td (12.1 Cable glands) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333 Td (The gateway enclosure has three cable entries on the underside. From left to right as viewed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 320 Td (from the front:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298 Td (- Entry 1: M20 x 1.5, for the Ethernet \(ETH0\) cable, cable diameter 6-12 mm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 285 Td (- Entry 2: M20 x 1.5, for the DC power cable, cable diameter 6-12 mm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272 Td (- Entry 3: M16 x 1.5, for the service or auxiliary I/O cable, cable diameter 4-8 mm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 259 Td (Unused entries must be closed with the blanking plugs provided. Tighten the gland cap nuts to 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 246 Td (N m for M20 glands and 2.5 N m for M16 glands to maintain the IP66 rating. From firmware 5.3.0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 233 Td (onwards, the gland kit TS4-GLD-KIT-02 replaces the older TS4-GLD-KIT-01; the new kit adds an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 220 Td (EMC gland for M20 entry 1, which is recommended where the Ethernet cable runs alongside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207 Td (variable-speed drive cabling.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 184 Td (12.2 Environmental limits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 162 Td (- Operating temperature: -30 to +70 C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 149 Td (- Storage temperature: -40 to +85 C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 136 Td (- Relative humidity: 5-95%, non-condensing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (- Ingress protection: IP66 with lid closed and all entries sealed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 110 Td (- Enclosure: UV-stabilised polycarbonate, 240 x 180 x 90 mm excluding antennas.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (A breather valve in the enclosure base equalises pressure. Do not paint over or block it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 72 Td (13. Time, buffering and connectivity behaviour) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
