stream
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 728 Td (13.1 Time synchronisation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 706 Td (The gateway synchronises its clock using NTP, by default from pool servers operated for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 693 Td (TesseraCloud \(time.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com\). A custom NTP server can be entered) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 680 Td (at System > Time > NTP Servers. If the clock drifts by more than 2 seconds relative to NTP, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 667 Td (gateway logs T-312 \(clock drift\). TLS connections to TesseraCloud fail when the gateway clock) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654 Td (is wrong by more than 24 hours, which typically happens only after a long power outage combined) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641 Td (with blocked NTP.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 618 Td (13.2 Heartbeats and offline status) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 596 Td (The gateway sends a heartbeat to TesseraCloud every 60 seconds. TesseraCloud marks the gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 583 Td (Offline after 10 consecutive missed heartbeats, that is, after 10 minutes without contact. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td (knowledge-base article covering offline gateways is available \(sup-kb-ts4-gateway-offline\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 547 Td (13.3 Store-and-forward buffer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 525 Td (When backhaul is unavailable, the gateway stores readings in a 256 MB flash buffer. At the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 512 Td (default reporting interval with 64 nodes, the buffer holds approximately 30 days of readings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 499 Td (When the buffer reaches 90% the gateway raises event T-348 \(buffer near capacity\); once full,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486 Td (the oldest readings are overwritten first. Buffered readings are uploaded automatically, oldest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 473 Td (first, when the connection is restored, at a rate of up to 2,000 readings per minute so that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 460 Td (live data is not delayed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 435 Td (14. Firmware updates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 413 Td (Gateway firmware is normally updated over the air from TesseraCloud \(Fleet > Gateways >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 400 Td ([gateway] > Firmware > Schedule Update\). Updates can also be applied locally from System >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 387 Td (Firmware > Upload in the local interface using a signed image file \(.tfw\) downloaded from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374 Td (Meridian partner portal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 352 Td (- An update takes approximately 6 minutes, including a reboot. Mesh traffic is buffered by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339 Td (   the nodes during the reboot.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326 Td (- The gateway uses A/B firmware partitions. If the new image fails to boot three times in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 313 Td (   succession, the gateway rolls back automatically to the previous version and logs the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300 Td (   rollback.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 287 Td (- Always check the compatibility matrix before updating. Node firmware 2.8.0 requires) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 274 Td (   gateway firmware 5.3.0. Updating nodes before their gateway will make them unable to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 261 Td (   rejoin.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248 Td (- Update the gateway first, then the nodes. Node updates are distributed over the mesh and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 235 Td (   take approximately 40 minutes per node at 1-hop, longer for deeper nodes; up to 8 nodes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (   are updated in parallel.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 206 Td (15. Factory reset) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 184 Td (A factory reset erases all configuration, including the mesh network ID, the paired node list,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 171 Td (network settings and the admin password. The device certificate is retained, so the gateway can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 158 Td (reconnect to TesseraCloud once backhaul is configured again, but all nodes must be re-paired.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 136 Td (To reset: with the gateway powered, press and hold the recessed RESET button beside the SVC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (port for 15 seconds, until the status LED flashes amber rapidly. Release the button. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 110 Td (gateway reboots with factory defaults, which takes about 90 seconds. A shorter press \(between 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (and 5 seconds\) only reboots the gateway without resetting it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 72 Td (16. Status LED reference) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
